<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11727" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crŭmēna</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crŭmīna</span></b> ),
			ae, f.
		for scrumena; root scru-, of scrutor, scrotum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small
			money-purse</i> or <i>bag</i> (usually hanging from
			the neck). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 3, 1, 7 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. As. 3,
				3, 63</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 3, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 1,
				2, 37</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, like our <i>purse</i>, for <i>money</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non deficiente crumenā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 4, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 11, 38</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
